From: Norbert Lange <nolange79@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2020 01:22:21 +0200
Subject: [Buildroot] [PATCH v2 1/1] package/pkg-meson: move crosscompilation
 support out of package
Message-ID: <20200929232221.469186-1-nolange79@gmail.com>
List-Id: <buildroot.busybox.net>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="us-ascii"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
To: buildroot@busybox.net

install the cross-compilation.conf file when setting up the
toolchain, not as part of host-meson.
This allows external usage of the buildroot toolchain through
meson, whether the host-meson package is built or not
(similar to other build systems like cmake).

Removed a few variables, as they were only used to communicate
between the meson package and pkg-meson.mk and are not needed
anymore. (Correctly prefix those with PKG_MESON_)

Prefer explicit Buildroot variables for compiler tools.

The sed pattern for cross-compilation.conf is now be generated by a function,
instead of being duplicated.

Signed-off-by: Norbert Lange <nolange79@gmail.com>
---
v1->v2:
-   squash 2 commits, really hard to separate as moving and renaming
    variables from 2 to one location affects alot code.
-   use TOOLCHAIN_POST_INSTALL_STAGING_HOOKS again.
-   consistently use double quotes for sed patterns

Signed-off-by: Norbert Lange <nolange79@gmail.com>
